INT. PICKLE FACTORY - HUMAN RESOURCES OFFICE - DAY

A glass cubicle overlooking the brine vats. The air is vinegar. A motivational poster reads: "BE THE DILL."

MAGDALENA OKOYE-FINNEGAN (50s, HR director, cardigan, sensible shoes) sits behind a desk stacked with folders. Across from her, BARRY KOWALSKI-ADEYEMI (40s, line supervisor, apron, spotless) folds his hands in his lap. In the corner, a chair holds PETRONELLA GRUBER (60s, union rep, thermos, knitting).

She smiles. He smiles back.

MAGDALENA
Thank you for coming in, Barry.

BARRY
Of course.

MAGDALENA
This is informal.

BARRY
Great.

She slides a folder across the desk. He does not touch it. Petronella knits.

MAGDALENA
Anything you'd like to share?

BARRY
About what?

MAGDALENA
Anything.

He glances at the folder. At Petronella. At the poster.

BARRY
Business is good.

MAGDALENA
Is it?

BARRY
Yes.

She nods. Opens the folder. Takes out a single photograph and sets it between them. He leans forward, then back, swallowing.

BARRY (CONT'D)
That's a gherkin.

MAGDALENA
It is.

BARRY
It's a small gherkin.

MAGDALENA
It is a small gherkin that was found in the Reuben line of Plant Three.

PETRONELLA
(not looking up)
Knit one, purl two.

BARRY
That's hardly my fault.

MAGDALENA
Whose fault is it?

BARRY
Systemic.

She closes the folder gently. Folds her hands.

MAGDALENA
Barry, we ran the camera footage.

His smile stays. Everything else drains. Petronella sets down her needles.

PETRONELLA
He did it for the cat.

MAGDALENA
(to Petronella)
Not now.

BARRY
It was a stray.

MAGDALENA
It ate forty pounds of relish.

BARRY
It was hungry.

Petronella pours tea into the thermos cap and offers it to him. He takes it.
